    abstract = {Recent experimental techniques used to investigate shear banding are reviewed. After recalling the rheological signature of shear-banded ﬂows, we summarize the various tools for measuring locally the microstructure and the velocity ﬁeld under shear. Local velocity measurements using dynamic light scattering and ultrasound are emphasized. A few results are extracted from current works to illustrate open questions and directions for future research.},
